  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39649006",
      "title": "How React Handles Components & How It Builds A \"Component Tree\" [Core Concept]",
      "sourceHash": "dbba710a987aaaa5bd459255bc8bfe529d0935f017a9001b058902f5b53d0c94",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.09,
          "end": 0.923,
          "en": "So now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 0.923,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "that we built a first custom component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "it's important to fully understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 11.73,
          "en": "how that component's content ended up on the website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.73,
          "end": 13.32,
          "en": "and our screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.32,
          "end": 16.32,
          "en": "So as a first step, let's go to the website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.32,
          "end": 20.253,
          "en": "and let's inspect the source code of that website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.09,
          "end": 25.56,
          "en": "If you do that, you'll note that you don't find the header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.56,
          "end": 29.13,
          "en": "or any other website content in that source code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.13,
          "end": 32.01,
          "en": "No image, no titles, nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.01,
          "end": 34.38,
          "en": "It just contains some metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.38,
          "end": 37.41,
          "en": "and at least one JavaScript import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.41,
          "end": 40.62,
          "en": "one JavaScript file that's being loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.62,
          "end": 43.83,
          "en": "But this loaded JavaScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.83,
          "end": 47.61,
          "en": "the index.jsx file in the end here in my case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.61,
          "end": 51.12,
          "en": "is the key because the code that is loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.12,
          "end": 53.94,
          "en": "and executed here is, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.94,
          "end": 57.57,
          "en": "the transformed React code you wrote.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.57,
          "end": 59.07,
          "en": "Remember I mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.07,
          "end": 61.68,
          "en": "that the code you write wouldn't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.68,
          "end": 63.39,
          "en": "like this in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.39,
          "end": 65.1,
          "en": "hence, it's transformed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 67.65,
          "en": "And it also shouldn't be too surprising",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.65,
          "end": 71.25,
          "en": "that we see the index.jsx file being loaded here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.25,
          "end": 73.68,
          "en": "in the actual website source code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.68,
          "end": 77.22,
          "en": "because that's also what we see here in our project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.22,
          "end": 79.35,
          "en": "in the index.html file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.35,
          "end": 83.37,
          "en": "And in the end, it is this index.html file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.37,
          "end": 86.28,
          "en": "that's being served to the website visitors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.28,
          "end": 87.72,
          "en": "Now, as you learned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.72,
          "end": 91.86,
          "en": "this index.jsx file does import something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.86,
          "end": 93.9,
          "en": "from the App.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.9,
          "end": 97.02000000000001,
          "en": "It imports the App component to be precise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 100.68,
          "en": "because it's that App component that's being exported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.68,
          "end": 102.87,
          "en": "in that App.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.87,
          "end": 105.33,
          "en": "By the way, this export keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.33,
          "end": 107.64,
          "en": "and this import keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.64,
          "end": 111,
          "en": "and this entire import-export feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111,
          "end": 113.7,
          "en": "is a regular JavaScript feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.7,
          "end": 116.37,
          "en": "It's not React-specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.37,
          "end": 119.88,
          "en": "So it's this App component function that's being imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.88,
          "end": 122.58,
          "en": "into the index.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.58,
          "end": 127.58,
          "en": "And in this file, it's being used as JSX code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.22,
          "end": 132.33,
          "en": "Now as you can see, we have no React component here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.33,
          "end": 136.59,
          "en": "This JSX code is not getting returned by some function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.59,
          "end": 139.05,
          "en": "Instead, it's getting used as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.05,
          "end": 141.99,
          "en": "as an argument for some other method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.99,
          "end": 144.84,
          "en": "that's being called here, the render method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.84,
          "end": 147.36,
          "en": "And indeed, as a React developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.36,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "you will almost exclusively use JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 153.32999999999998,
          "en": "inside of component functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.32999999999998,
          "end": 154.59,
          "en": "What we see here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.59,
          "end": 159.18,
          "en": "in the index.jsx file is the one important exception",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.18,
          "end": 163.5,
          "en": "because this file, this index.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.5,
          "end": 168.5,
          "en": "acts as the main entry point of our React app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.07999999999998,
          "end": 174.03,
          "en": "since it is the first file to be loaded by the HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.03,
          "end": 175.77,
          "en": "And it's in this place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.77,
          "end": 179.91,
          "en": "where the React app boots up, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.91,
          "end": 184.35,
          "en": "To be precise, it's this special React DOM library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.35,
          "end": 188.07,
          "en": "which in the end belongs to the overall React library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.07,
          "end": 189.96,
          "en": "from which we're importing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.96,
          "end": 193.89,
          "en": "which ultimately renders this App component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.89,
          "end": 195.24,
          "en": "So, which is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.24,
          "end": 199.41,
          "en": "for outputting the App component's content on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.41,
          "end": 200.82,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 200.82,
          "end": 203.01,
          "en": "And this App component is rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 206.76,
          "en": "by passing JSX code to this render method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 206.76,
          "end": 211.5,
          "en": "This render method, however, is being called on an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.5,
          "end": 216.017,
          "en": "that's created with another method, the createRoot method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.05,
          "end": 222.05,
          "en": "This method takes an existing HTML element as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 222.42000000000002,
          "end": 225.72,
          "en": "so an element that's not being created by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 225.72,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "but that instead is part of the index.html file already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 235.28,
          "en": "In this case, that would be this div here with the id root,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.55,
          "end": 240.84,
          "en": "since that's what we're selecting here with getElementById,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.84,
          "end": 245.28,
          "en": "that's what's getting passed to this createRoot method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.28,
          "end": 248.94,
          "en": "And then with that element selected and set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.94,
          "end": 251.94,
          "en": "as a root for the React project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 251.94,
          "end": 256.32,
          "en": "React goes ahead and injects a React component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 256.32,
          "end": 258.63,
          "en": "the App component in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.63,
          "end": 260.67,
          "en": "into this element, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 260.67,
          "end": 264.15,
          "en": "It renders this component and all its contents,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.15,
          "end": 267.18,
          "en": "including any nested components it may contain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.18,
          "end": 271.02,
          "en": "and their content into this div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.02,
          "end": 273.39,
          "en": "That's what this render method does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.39,
          "end": 278.04,
          "en": "And that's why if you open the developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 278.04,
          "end": 281.07,
          "en": "and there the elements tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281.07,
          "end": 285.96,
          "en": "you see more than just the initial HTML structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.96,
          "end": 287.94,
          "en": "Instead, you see all the elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 287.94,
          "end": 290.49,
          "en": "that are indeed visible on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 290.49,
          "end": 294.65999999999997,
          "en": "and you see that they are inside of that div here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 294.65999999999997,
          "end": 296.43,
          "en": "with the id root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 296.43,
          "end": 298.77,
          "en": "So the header and the main section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 298.77,
          "end": 301.32,
          "en": "which is in the end simply the content defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.32,
          "end": 304.89,
          "en": "in the App component and our custom Header component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.89,
          "end": 308.64,
          "en": "are inside of that div with the id root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 308.64,
          "end": 312.84,
          "en": "So the createRoot and render methods are responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 312.84,
          "end": 315.36,
          "en": "for rendering a single root component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 315.36,
          "end": 317.52,
          "en": "the App component in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 317.52,
          "end": 319.56,
          "en": "which then in turn may contain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 319.56,
          "end": 322.68,
          "en": "as many nested components as needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 322.68,
          "end": 324.42,
          "en": "And those nested components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 324.42,
          "end": 328.35,
          "en": "it may include like this Header component in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 328.35,
          "end": 331.62,
          "en": "could then contain even more child components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 331.62,
          "end": 332.90999999999997,
          "en": "And with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 332.90999999999997,
          "end": 337.02,
          "en": "ultimately you end up with a component hierarchy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 337.02,
          "end": 340.32,
          "en": "which is often called a tree of components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 340.32,
          "end": 342.27,
          "en": "a structure of components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 342.27,
          "end": 345.87,
          "en": "which is then rendered to the screen via React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 345.87,
          "end": 348.65999999999997,
          "en": "But what's important to understand about this tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 348.65999999999997,
          "end": 352.23,
          "en": "of components and components in general is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 352.23,
          "end": 355.68,
          "en": "that your custom components are not showing up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 355.68,
          "end": 358.62,
          "en": "in the actual rendered DOM though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 358.62,
          "end": 362.7,
          "en": "There you only find default HTML elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 362.7,
          "end": 365.61,
          "en": "for example, here, the header with the lowercase h,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 365.61,
          "end": 368.04,
          "en": "which is the built-in header element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 368.04,
          "end": 372.54,
          "en": "not our custom component, which had an uppercase H.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 372.54,
          "end": 376.26,
          "en": "We also don't see the App component in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 376.26,
          "end": 378.42,
          "en": "So your tree of components is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 378.42,
          "end": 381.33,
          "en": "in the end, just analyzed by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 381.33,
          "end": 384.84,
          "en": "And React then combines all the JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 384.84,
          "end": 389.64,
          "en": "from all those components to generate the overall DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 389.64,
          "end": 393.12,
          "en": "the elements that are showing up on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 393.12,
          "end": 396.6,
          "en": "But as a developer, you have the convenience of working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 396.6,
          "end": 399.24,
          "en": "with those individual building blocks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 399.24,
          "end": 402.48,
          "en": "instead of a single potentially huge file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 402.48,
          "end": 405.06,
          "en": "that contains all the markup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 405.06,
          "end": 406.65,
          "en": "And you can now also see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 406.65,
          "end": 410.07,
          "en": "why your component function names must start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 410.07,
          "end": 412.2,
          "en": "with an uppercase character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 412.2,
          "end": 417.2,
          "en": "All built-in elements like div, image, or header start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 417.48,
          "end": 420.57,
          "en": "with lowercase characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 420.57,
          "end": 422.82,
          "en": "Custom components on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 422.82,
          "end": 427.82,
          "en": "so components built by you or other developers must start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 427.95,
          "end": 430.02,
          "en": "with an uppercase character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 430.02,
          "end": 434.19,
          "en": "to tell React that it's not a built-in component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 434.19,
          "end": 437.46,
          "en": "So that's how React tells custom components apart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 437.46,
          "end": 439.203,
          "en": "from built-in components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 440.13,
          "end": 443.82,
          "en": "This does not just prevent potential name clashes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 443.82,
          "end": 448.5,
          "en": "like for example here where header with a lowercase h,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 448.5,
          "end": 451.68,
          "en": "would clash with the builtin header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 451.68,
          "end": 455.4,
          "en": "But it also changes how React handles a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 455.4,
          "end": 460.4,
          "en": "Built-in components like header, image, div, and so on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 460.44,
          "end": 464.67,
          "en": "are rendered as DOM nodes by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 464.67,
          "end": 465.63,
          "en": "On the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 465.63,
          "end": 470.04,
          "en": "custom components like our Header here are just functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 470.04,
          "end": 473.67,
          "en": "and are therefore executed as functions by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 473.67,
          "end": 476.67,
          "en": "And it then just takes a look at them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 476.67,
          "end": 480.57,
          "en": "takes the returned value, the returned JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 480.57,
          "end": 484.14,
          "en": "and starts analyzing that code until it ends up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 484.14,
          "end": 488.19,
          "en": "with only built-in elements at a certain point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 488.19,
          "end": 490.92,
          "en": "which are then rendered to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 490.92,
          "end": 493.11,
          "en": "And that's how React works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 493.11,
          "end": 495.69,
          "en": "how it uses those components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 495.69,
          "end": 499.953,
          "en": "and how it ultimately renders them onto the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
